against Iran, including the Strait of Hormuz blockade. Trump reaffirmed the trip yesterday at the White House Small Business Summit, calling it a \\\"very important\\\" opportunity to discuss trade stability, technology competition, and avoiding escalation amid tariffs and Taiwan tensions. Today's visit by Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi to meet Chinese Foreign Minister Wang Yi underscores Beijing's balancing act as a potential mediator, with analysts viewing it as coordination to protect Tehran's interests ahead of the bilateral talks. No major cancellations signal risks, though Iran war developments could prompt further delays.\",\"context_requires_regen\":false,\"context_updated_at\":\"2026-05-06T05:01:10.152Z\"}}],\"pagination\":{\"hasMore\":true,\"totalResults\":3328}}\n"
